Take `N` the splitting field of `X^M − π` (Galois: `Kᵥ` has
characteristic zero), i.e. `N = Kᵥ(μ_M, z)`. Then
`e(N/Kᵥ) = e(N/Kᵥ(μ_M)) = M`, because `Kᵥ(μ_M)/Kᵥ` is unramified while
